\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Per-run metrics at full recorded precision for every training run in this work --- the two frozen campaigns and the mean-teacher positive control --- on both endpoints. Arms B and C10 appear once; they were re-scored, not re-trained, for the falsification campaign and reproduced their committed values exactly at six decimal places. \emph  {Source:} \texttt  {rebuild/ABC/out/abc\_metrics.csv} and \texttt  {out/t2/abc\_metrics.csv}; blocks \texttt  {EXP ABC} \#3 and \texttt  {EXP T2} \#3.}}{24}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:perrun}{{6}{24}{Per-run metrics at full recorded precision for every training run in this work --- the two frozen campaigns and the mean-teacher positive control --- on both endpoints. Arms B and C10 appear once; they were re-scored, not re-trained, for the falsification campaign and reproduced their committed values exactly at six decimal places. \emph {Source:} \texttt {rebuild/ABC/out/abc\_metrics.csv} and \texttt {out/t2/abc\_metrics.csv}; blocks \texttt {EXP ABC} \#3 and \texttt {EXP T2} \#3}{table.6}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Which evaluation columns can be reported as independent measurements. Every rate is still a \emph  {lower bound}: different photographs of one specimen, montages and heavy colour edits are not detected, and an image with no match is unchecked, not clean. The CHAMELEON row combines the released same-dimension detector's $41$ with $9$ rescaled or cropped copies recovered by the geometric extension and confirmed by post-warp residual; the other three rows are same-dimension only, so their unchecked shares are larger than stated here. In the exact-hash column $0$ is a measured zero against the \emph  {training pool}, ``---'' not applicable; it is not a claim about overlap between benchmarks (Section~\ref {sec:contamination}). $^{\ddagger }$the nearest-neighbour gap is evidence for the same-dimension tier of $41$, not for the combined figure. \emph  {Source:} \texttt  {CLEAN\_PROTOCOL.md}; \texttt  {EXP D2} \#5, \texttt  {D2R} \#4, \texttt  {D2\_NC4K} \#2; extension and adjudication in \texttt  {rebuild/FINAL\_AUDIT/out/final\_verdicts.json}.}}{25}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:contamination}{{7}{25}{Which evaluation columns can be reported as independent measurements. Every rate is still a \emph {lower bound}: different photographs of one specimen, montages and heavy colour edits are not detected, and an image with no match is unchecked, not clean. The CHAMELEON row combines the released same-dimension detector's $41$ with $9$ rescaled or cropped copies recovered by the geometric extension and confirmed by post-warp residual; the other three rows are same-dimension only, so their unchecked shares are larger than stated here. In the exact-hash column $0$ is a measured zero against the \emph {training pool}, ``---'' not applicable; it is not a claim about overlap between benchmarks (Section~\ref {sec:contamination}). $^{\ddagger }$the nearest-neighbour gap is evidence for the same-dimension tier of $41$, not for the combined figure. \emph {Source:} \texttt {CLEAN\_PROTOCOL.md}; \texttt {EXP D2} \#5, \texttt {D2R} \#4, \texttt {D2\_NC4K} \#2; extension and adjudication in \texttt {rebuild/FINAL\_AUDIT/out/final\_verdicts.json}}{table.7}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Post-hoc interval estimates for the gaps this paper turns on, on COD10K-test $S_\alpha $. \emph  {These decide nothing}: the verdicts remain the pre-registered $2\hat  {\sigma }$ rule of Section~\ref {sec:setup}, which reports no $p$-value at $n=3$. Intervals are Welch (unequal-variance) on the two arms actually compared, so they are not inflated by A0. TOST is run at the SESOI $\delta = 0.005$; the final column gives the smallest $\delta $ at which each comparison \emph  {could} have concluded equivalence, which is the honest positive statement the data supports. \emph  {Source:} \texttt  {rebuild/DIAG/out/diag\_tost.json}.}}{25}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:tost}{{8}{25}{Post-hoc interval estimates for the gaps this paper turns on, on COD10K-test $S_\alpha $. \emph {These decide nothing}: the verdicts remain the pre-registered $2\hat {\sigma }$ rule of Section~\ref {sec:setup}, which reports no $p$-value at $n=3$. Intervals are Welch (unequal-variance) on the two arms actually compared, so they are not inflated by A0. TOST is run at the SESOI $\delta = 0.005$; the final column gives the smallest $\delta $ at which each comparison \emph {could} have concluded equivalence, which is the honest positive statement the data supports. \emph {Source:} \texttt {rebuild/DIAG/out/diag\_tost.json}}{table.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The ten most-funded clusters, and what the budget is actually aimed at. The target pool is $24.8\%$ CAMO, but $51.5\%$ of the generation budget lands on CAMO images --- a $2.08\times $ enrichment ($2.14\times $ under the committed assignment). The two largest quotas take $33.5\%$ of the budget, are $90.2\%$ CAMO, and between them hold $7$ of the $2026$ primary-endpoint images. \emph  {Source:} \texttt  {rebuild/DIAG/out/diag\_clusters.json}.}}{26}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:clustercomp}{{9}{26}{The ten most-funded clusters, and what the budget is actually aimed at. The target pool is $24.8\%$ CAMO, but $51.5\%$ of the generation budget lands on CAMO images --- a $2.08\times $ enrichment ($2.14\times $ under the committed assignment). The two largest quotas take $33.5\%$ of the budget, are $90.2\%$ CAMO, and between them hold $7$ of the $2026$ primary-endpoint images. \emph {Source:} \texttt {rebuild/DIAG/out/diag\_clusters.json}}{table.9}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Arm differences on \emph  {boundary} metrics, COD10K-test, same three seeds, same pooled-$\hat  {\sigma }$ rule. \textbf  {Post-hoc: these metrics were not pre-registered and no campaign verdict is re-decided.} On SINet the concentration gap $\mathrm  {C10}-\mathrm  {B}$ clears its bar --- and so does $\mathrm  {CINV}-\mathrm  {B}$, the \emph  {anti}-targeted arm, by as much; the two direction contrasts stay within noise. SINet-v2 resolves none of it, and that disagreement is reported as a disagreement. \emph  {Source:} \texttt  {rebuild/DIAG/out/diag\_subgroups.json}.}}{26}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:boundary}{{10}{26}{Arm differences on \emph {boundary} metrics, COD10K-test, same three seeds, same pooled-$\hat {\sigma }$ rule. \textbf {Post-hoc: these metrics were not pre-registered and no campaign verdict is re-decided.} On SINet the concentration gap $\mathrm {C10}-\mathrm {B}$ clears its bar --- and so does $\mathrm {CINV}-\mathrm {B}$, the \emph {anti}-targeted arm, by as much; the two direction contrasts stay within noise. SINet-v2 resolves none of it, and that disagreement is reported as a disagreement. \emph {Source:} \texttt {rebuild/DIAG/out/diag\_subgroups.json}}{table.10}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Every cause, its measured quantity, and how far it carries. Causes marked \emph  {generalizes} concern the target data or the uncertainty signal and travel beyond this instantiation; those marked \emph  {specific to this setup} are properties of this loop or this generator. The scope column, not the magnitude column, determines how far a row may be carried. \emph  {Sources, by row:} \texttt  {FINAL\_RESULTS.md} Tables 8.2, 8.1, 9.2, 9.4, 11.1, 12.1, 5.1, 7.1 and 10.4; blocks \texttt  {EXP B1} \#3 and \#4, \texttt  {EXP C1} \#4, \texttt  {EXP T2} \#3, \texttt  {EXP T2C}, \texttt  {EXP ABC} \#2, \texttt  {EXP D1}, \texttt  {EXP A3}, in \texttt  {results/REBUILD\_LOG.txt}. The conditioning row has no log block by construction.}}{27}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:causes}{{11}{27}{Every cause, its measured quantity, and how far it carries. Causes marked \emph {generalizes} concern the target data or the uncertainty signal and travel beyond this instantiation; those marked \emph {specific to this setup} are properties of this loop or this generator. The scope column, not the magnitude column, determines how far a row may be carried. \emph {Sources, by row:} \texttt {FINAL\_RESULTS.md} Tables 8.2, 8.1, 9.2, 9.4, 11.1, 12.1, 5.1, 7.1 and 10.4; blocks \texttt {EXP B1} \#3 and \#4, \texttt {EXP C1} \#4, \texttt {EXP T2} \#3, \texttt {EXP T2C}, \texttt {EXP ABC} \#2, \texttt {EXP D1}, \texttt {EXP A3}, in \texttt {results/REBUILD\_LOG.txt}. The conditioning row has no log block by construction}{table.11}{}}
